**Check the abort signal again right before the spawn.**

The late abort check runs at Line 452. After that check, the run awaits several steps before the spawn at Line 592: `store.create`/`resumedRecordOrThrow`, `appendMessage`, `buildManifest`, `readCliSessionId` and `writeMcpConfig`. An abort can fire during any of them. The code still spawns the CLI and writes the prompt to stdin. The listener check at Line 690 then starts termination for a child that is already running. The default `termGraceMs` window is the time the CLI gets before SIGTERM takes effect. In that window, the CLI can already send the provider request.

This conflicts with two rules:
- The header says an already-aborted signal "never dispatches" (cli.ts:17).
- The path instruction says cancellation "must actually stop client-side spend".

The session record already exists at this point, so return an `'aborted'` verdict that carries `sessionId`. Also remove the MCP config. Keep the check at Line 690. Nothing between the spawn and that check can interleave, so it stays a valid backstop.

